GEO:39.169144;-86.519739
SUMMARY:Writing in the Galleries
DESCRIPTION:Spark your creative writing through close looking and convers
 ation. Together\, we'll explore the observations and questions sparked by
  this painting\, then allow individual time for reflective writing to eac
 h bring our own perspective.&#160\;  Whether you're a writer or simply cu
 rious to try something new\, you'll find inspiration here and a welcoming
  community to share the journey.  What to Bringyour favorite pencil (no p
 ens).  a notebook or paper. Clipboards are available to borrow.  a phone 
 or camera to take a picture of the art for later reference.    &#160\;Kno
 w Before You GoArrive early\, check in\, and get ready for an on-time sta
 rt.Readwhere to find us\, where to park\, accessibility\, and museum guid
 elines.About Your Facilitator  Dedaimia Whitney earned an MFA in fiction 
 from Indiana University under the direction of Scott Russell Sanders. She
  taught creative writing at Franklin College for many years. She has serv
 ed the museum as a docent since 2019. Her favorite works of art are those
  that are both visually stimulating and thought-provoking.
