LOCATION:GLOBAL &amp\; INTERNATIONAL STUDIES BUILDING
GEO:39.170002;-86.517492
SUMMARY:Global Competencies Skills Development Series: Disaster Response\
 , Humanitarian Systems & Crisis Leadership Dinner
DESCRIPTION:Directing Responses in the World's Complex Crises  When natur
 al disasters\, complex emergencies\, or global health crises strike\, how
  do international humanitarian systems deploy aid\, manage logistics\, an
 d make high-stakes choices on the ground?  Join the Global Competencies S
 kills Development Series for an intimate\, off-the-record conversation wi
 th Michael Jack—former USAID Bureau for Humanitarian Assistance Divisio
 n Director\, international disaster management strategist\, and certified
  leadership coach.  Michael has served on the front lines of major U.S. g
 overnment international disaster responses\, including the Iraq Sinjar cr
 isis\, West Africa Ebola outbreak\, Mexico City earthquake\, South Sudan 
 complex emergency\, Amazon wildfires\, and the Northern Ethiopia response
 .  Skip high-level theory. This session breaks down raw operational trade
 craft: leading cross-agency disaster systems\, managing risk under extrem
 e uncertainty\, and building the personal stamina required for high-stake
 s international careers.  &#160\;
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<h4 data-path-to-node="14">  Directing Respo
 nses in the World's Complex Crises</h4><p data-path-to-node="15">  When n
 atural disasters\, complex emergencies\, or global health crises strike\,
  how do international humanitarian systems deploy aid\, manage logistics\
 , and make high-stakes choices on the ground?</p><p data-path-to-node="16
 ">  Join the <strong data-path-to-node="16" data-index-in-node="9">Global
  Competencies Skills Development Series</strong> for an intimate\, off-th
 e-record conversation with <strong data-path-to-node="16" data-index-in-n
 ode="105">Michael Jack</strong>—former USAID Bureau for Humanitarian As
 sistance Division Director\, international disaster management strategist
 \, and certified leadership coach.</p><p data-path-to-node="17">  Michael
  has served on the front lines of major U.S. government international dis
 aster responses\, including the <strong data-path-to-node="17" data-index
 -in-node="111">Iraq Sinjar crisis\, West Africa Ebola outbreak\, Mexico C
 ity earthquake\, South Sudan complex emergency\, Amazon wildfires\, and t
 he Northern Ethiopia response</strong>.</p><p data-path-to-node="18">  Sk
 ip high-level theory. This session breaks down raw operational tradecraft
 : leading cross-agency disaster systems\, managing risk under extreme unc
 ertainty\, and building the personal stamina required for high-stakes int
 ernational careers.</p><h4 data-path-to-node="19">  &#160\;</h4>
